title: '"diff-view: order-only changes"'
pid: 9b99374a-1b10-40fb-8054-88e3f7891db2
body: |2-
  A flat list, in ID order, of the nodes whose only change is the order
  of some list: their only leaf is their other changes ("Other changes
  to a node's file"), each of them a reorder
  ('ChangeLeaves::order_only_pids'). Each is shown with its other
  changes, the headline that shows the old order against the new and
  takes the mark, then its content in the new order, as write-protected
  members shown without their content. Its sets are empty: it renders
  no pruned change view. Such a node is in C, so the all-changes buffer
  shows it too, the same way.
